   "en": "Go down the Tsarist Russia route. Win the civil war. (It helps a lot to practice infiltration aggressively: preferably, you should have infiltrated every state along the Trans-Siberian Railway as far as Chelyabinsk and Akhtubinsk by the time you start the civil war.) Release the peripheral states as puppets. The only places where this won't work (your border runs through your core states that can't be released) are 1) Krasnoyarsk, and 2) Leningrad and adjacent states. You will need to go to war with Tannu Tuva, Finland, Latvia, and Estonia to annex them before they can be puppeted. The biggest complication is that Latvia and Estonia might join the Allies (or the Triple Entente) before you have a chance to annex them, so you need to rush down the focuses and get them before it's too late."
